"early_entry_card" = "EARLY ENTRY CLIENT CARD: ?????\n\nExpires on: ~~~~~\n\nClient: _____\n\nExpress entry is available only for arrivals between 2:00 PM and 2:30 PM. Arrivals after this window will be numbered in the order received, alongside other clients.\n\n**Early entry for medical reasons requires a doctor’s note.**\n\nThis card is non-transferable.\n\nDate issued:** -----**";
"early_entry_label" = "Early Entry";
"early_entry_text" = "**Early Entry** is a service for persons 65 and older and persons who have difficulty standing for an extended period of time. You will be granted access to the ***4 K.I.D.S. Sake*** food pantry 30 minutes before the general public.\n\nTo access this service, you must either:\n\n1) Prove you are at least 65 years old (State ID, Drivers License, etc.)\n\n2) Present a note from your doctor confirming your inability to stand for extended periods of time. A Social Security disability statement or a handicap parking permit does not quality. The doctor’s note should be HIPAA compliant and simply indicate such. We don’t need to know why. ***The doctor’s note must be reconfirmed each calendar year.***\n\nPresent your documentation to the front desk when you sign in.";
"feel_good_deals_label" = "Feel Good Deals";
"language_label" = "Language";
"lining_up_label" = "Process for lining up";
"lining_up_text" = "Persons 65 or older and disabled clients may form a line starting at 1:45. Numbers are passed out to these clients at 2:00.\n\nAll other families may start to form a line no earlier than 2:15. If the elderly/disabled line has NOT been processed, this line may be delayed until 2:30. Numbers are passed out to all other families beginning at 2:30.\n\nArriving early does NOT entitle you to earlier services, nor does any other lines formed to obtain numbers. All clients are asked to wait in their vehicles until their appropriate time.\n\nAll who receive a number will be offered the opportunity to shop. After 5:30, NO more numbers are passed out.\n\nTypically, about 25 clients are able to shop per hour. You may wait in your vehicle, but you must return before your number is called—no later than 5:30.\n\nFollowing the rules is essential. Running, pushing, or jumping in front of others will result in a loss of service for that day. Repeated offenses will result in a permanent ban on our services.\n\nThese rules may be changed from time to time as necessary.";
